1
00:01:57,391 --> 00:02:03,391
Encanto at the Hollywood Bowl is a music,
documentary film directed by Chris Howe.

2
00:03:54,782 --> 00:04:00,782
Step into Casa Madrigal for a special concert spectacular as the original voice cast of Disney Animation's Oscar®-winning "Encanto," Stephanie Beatriz, Adassa, Carolina Gaitán, Jessica Darrow, Diane Guerrero, Mauro Castillo, Angie Cepeda and Olga Merediz,
along with special guests including Colombian superstar Carlos Vives, reunites for "Encanto at the Hollywood Bowl." This unprecedented concert experience gives you a front-row seat to the musical extravaganza celebrating the global phenomenon.

3
00:05:52,173 --> 00:05:58,173
Self - Host, played by Lin-Manuel Miranda.

4
00:07:49,565 --> 00:07:55,565
Mirabel Madrigal, played by Stephanie Beatriz.

5
00:09:46,956 --> 00:09:52,956
Dolores Madrigal, played by Adassa.

6
00:11:44,347 --> 00:11:50,347
Pepa Madrigal, played by Carolina Gaitán.

7
00:13:41,739 --> 00:13:47,739
Luisa Madrigal, played by Jess Darrow.

8
00:15:39,130 --> 00:15:45,130
Isabela Madrigal, played by Diane Guerrero.

9
00:17:36,521 --> 00:17:42,521
Encanto is a 2021 American animated musical fantasy comedy
film produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios.

10
00:19:33,913 --> 00:19:39,913
It was directed by Jared Bush, and Byron Howard and written by Charise Castro Smith and Bush, with
original songs written by Lin-Manuel Miranda and a score composed by Germaine Franco.

11
00:21:31,304 --> 00:21:37,304
The film stars the voices of Stephanie Beatriz, María Cecilia Botero, John Leguizamo, Mauro Castillo,
Jessica Darrow, Angie Cepeda, Carolina Gaitán, Diane Guerrero, and Wilmer Valderrama.

12
00:23:28,695 --> 00:23:34,695
Encanto follows a multigenerational Colombian family, the Madrigals, led by a matriarch whose children and grandchildren—except for Mirabel
Madrigal—receive magical gifts from a miracle, which they use to help the people in their rural community, called the Encanto.

13
00:25:26,086 --> 00:25:32,086
When Mirabel learns that the family is losing their magic, she sets
out to find out why and save the family and house.

14
00:27:23,478 --> 00:27:29,478
Encanto premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on November 3, 2021, and
was released in the United States on November 24 over a 30-day theatrical run.

15
00:29:20,869 --> 00:29:26,869
It was also released in RealD 3D, Dolby Cinema, 2D and D-BOX formats.

16
00:31:18,260 --> 00:31:24,260
Despite underperformance at the box office, grossing $261.3 million worldwide against a $120–150
million budget, it was a ratings success after its release on Disney+ on December 24, 2021.

17
00:33:15,652 --> 00:33:21,652
The film received acclaim for its characterization, music, animation, voice acting, emotional depth, and cultural
fidelity; reviews named magic realism and transgenerational trauma as the film's core concepts.

18
00:35:13,043 --> 00:35:19,043
Publications have described Encanto as a cultural phenomenon, and executives had
begun referring to it as a "franchise" within a year of release.

19
00:37:10,434 --> 00:37:16,434
The film was nominated for three awards at the 94th Academy Awards, winning Best Animated Feature, and received numerous other
accolades, including the Golden Globe Award for Best Animated Feature and the BAFTA Award for Best Animated Film.

20
00:39:07,826 --> 00:39:13,826
The film's associated merchandise has seen significant success, and its soundtrack became a breakout sensation, reaching number one on the US Billboard 200 and UK Compilation Albums charts; "We Don't
Talk About Bruno" and "Surface Pressure" were its two most successful songs, with the former topping both the US Billboard Hot 100 and UK Singles Chart for multiple consecutive weeks.

21
00:41:05,217 --> 00:41:11,217
A theme park attraction based on the film is set to
open at Disney's Animal Kingdom in 2027.

22
00:43:02,608 --> 00:43:08,608
The film explores themes of concert, tv special, musical
adaptation, music concert, live concert.
